(δ + θ) + (π − q) = π ⟹ δ + θ = q ⟹ δ = q − θ = (φ−θ)/2 = p

**Collinearity constraint.** Since D = (R cos θ, R cos θ · tan p) lies on line CE, substituting into the parametric line from C to E yields (after algebra):

